## Fix Neo4j connection dropped by the UC-save payload (KG tab)

Context:
The Knowledge Graph tab's Neo4j Connection still did not stick. Root cause was a
second, hand-rolled `/domain/info` payload: `saveDomainInfoBeforeSave()` in
`navbar.js` (the auto-save that runs before every UC save) sent `graph_backend`
but not `neo4j_connection`. Since `Domain.save_domain_info` falls back to the
stored value for absent keys, the user's pick was silently discarded — and on a
domain that had no connection yet the fallback was blank, so the server rejected
the save. The Information form's Save button routes through `domainSave()`, so it
hit this path and never reached the guard added to `saveDomainInfo()`.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js`
   Extracted `buildDomainInfoPayload()` as the single source of truth for the
   `/domain/info` payload (now including `neo4j_connection`, cleared when the
   backend is not Neo4j) and made `saveDomainInfoBeforeSave()` use it. Added
   `validateDomainInfoForm()` and called it at the top of `domainSave()` so the
   "pick a connection" guard applies to the UC-save path too.
2. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js`
   `saveDomainInfo()` now builds its payload with the shared helper and defers to
   the shared validator, removing the duplicated field list that drifted.
3. `tests/units/domain/test_domain_neo4j_connection_picker.py`
   New `TestDomainInfoPayloadSharing`: the shared builder carries
   `neo4j_connection`, both save paths use it, no second field list remains in
   the UC-save path, and `domainSave()` validates before posting.

