## Fix Neo4j connection picker race with the page's own info re-fetch

Context:
The previous fix made the Save payload correct, but the connection still did
not stick for some users. Isolated the backend save→close→load-from-registry
round trip with direct API calls (curl, real workspace) and it persisted
correctly every time — so the loss was purely client-side. Reproduced with a
browser agent using the full real journey (open existing domain → pick
connection → Save → Close → reopen from the registry list): `#domainGraphBackend`
and `#domainNeo4jDatabase` are rendered correctly by the server-side Jinja
template on page load, but `domain-information.js`'s `DOMContentLoaded` handler
also re-fetches `/domain/info` inside a `Promise.all` gated behind
`loadLlmEndpoints()` — a real-workspace model-serving-endpoints call that can
take several seconds. When that fetch resolved, it unconditionally overwrote
both fields with the pre-page-load values. A user who picked a new backend or
connection before the slow fetch resolved had the pick silently reverted with
no warning; Save then reported success while persisting the stale value.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js`
   Both fields get a `dataset.userEdited = '1'` flag on their first `change`
   event, wired up before the slow `Promise.all` starts. The late `/domain/info`
   handler now skips overwriting a field once that flag is set, so a fresh user
   edit always wins over the stale re-fetch.
2. `tests/units/domain/test_domain_neo4j_connection_picker.py`
   New `TestNeo4jFieldEditRaceGuard`: dirty flags are wired for both fields
   before the `Promise.all`, and the late-fetch handler's overwrite is guarded
   by `!<field>.dataset.userEdited` immediately before each assignment.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
- tests/units/domain/test_domain_neo4j_connection_picker.py
- changelogs/v0.7.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-07.log

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 4785 passed, 276 skipped,
5 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 38.95s.

Verified in-browser (dedicated subagent, real workspace):
- Backend round trip (save-to-uc → close → load-from-uc via direct API calls)
  persisted `neo4j_connection` correctly on every attempt — confirms the loss
  was purely client-side.
- Reproduced the exact race with artificial network delay: picking a new
  Graph Backend / Neo4j Connection immediately after page load survived the
  later `/domain/info` + LLM-endpoints resolution (dropdowns kept the pick,
  `dataset.userEdited` was `"1"` on both fields, and the Save payload carried
  the picked connection, not the stale one). A subsequent fresh reload showed
  the persisted value with no console errors.

