## Fix scenario 3 graph-analysis timeout; add Ontos Integration to the v0.8.0 roadmap

Context:
Full validation pass: the non-scenario suite was green, but the live scenario
campaign failed on scenario 3 with `graph analysis did not finish within 300s`.
Investigation showed the app was healthy: the graph-analysis step delegates to
the `ontobricks-<instance>-graph-analytics` Lakeflow job, and Databricks run
591217018872608 finished SUCCESS in 596s (setup 5s, execution 590s) on the
52k-triple scenario graph. Scenario 3 was the only step budgeting an external
Databricks job, yet it had the smallest allowance (300s) — smaller than the
in-process build (420s), reasoning (420s) and rules (600s) steps, and 12x
smaller than the app's own `analytics_job_timeout_s` (3600s). The test gave up
while the job was still running normally. Separately, the August roadmap gained
an Ontos Integration entry under v0.8.0.

Changes:

1. `tests/e2e/scenarios/test_scenario_03_rules_analysis.py`
   Raised the `ONTOBRICKS_SCENARIO_ANALYSIS_TIMEOUT` default from 300s to 900s
   so the poll budget covers Lakeflow cluster start plus Spark centrality
   compute, with a comment recording the measured ~600s run and the app-side
   3600s allowance. Updated the module docstring's documented default.
2. `releases/Roadmap_2026-08.md`
   Added Ontos Integration to v0.8.0: executive-summary axis (five axes → six),
   a Known-limitations bullet, new "Pillar 8 — Ontos Integration" (P1), a
   Feature Matrix row, an updated v0.8.0 section title/theme, and Open Question
